Expected elements: present

Every must-show item renders and no must-not-show item appears: identity bar with `← aztec-testnet`, `0x0858d6…7fb2`, `Succeeded`, `block 63675`, both-direction stepping, `128 / 345`, phase rail; the `DATA` / `Real Aztec testnet data` provenance row with endpoint, capture moment and replay window; instruction-level explanations in Code, Call Trace and Values in their own words; `Supply sources`. No invented source, no fixture content, no blank pane.

**Cost row measured — the regression is REFUTED here.** Rules bound the row at y=542 and y=588: **46px**. Sibling rows measure 30px (BLOCK, TYPE) and 32px (AGE, CANONICAL, FINALITY). That is **1.53× the 30px text row, 1.44× the 32px badge row** — below the 1.6× baseline the claim cites, not 2.2–2.3×. The label `COST · TRANSACTION FEE` sets on ONE line (x1542–1695, 153px) with a 53px gap before the value; nothing wraps. Two lines total, both in the value column: digits, then `mana (FeeJuice)`. The 380px pane gives the label room the mainnet grid evidently does not.

Also resolved: the fee is a formatted decimal with a unit, not the raw hex the block predicted. The pane fade works — `"hydrationRounds": 6,` washes out and its descenders meet the edge; the pane plainly continues.

Hierarchy is the weak axis. In the Transaction pane the pane title, section headings and field labels share one 9px-cap uppercase level at identical ink, so 14 rows read flat.

Highest-priority fixes: separate section headings from field labels; group `128 / 345` with the stepping controls.

Rating: 6/10

